## STOP — read these before you touch anything

You are not done onboarding until you have **opened and read** every item below and can
**state what each one says**. Not "I am familiar with this". Not "standard practice". The
files are short and they contradict generic defaults in ways that will make your first
change wrong if you skim them.

Before your first edit in this repo, say out loud:

1. what the licence is here and what header a new file gets;
2. which command runs the gates, and what its coverage floor is;
3. one rule from the remediation procedure you would otherwise have broken.

If you cannot answer those from having read the files, you have not read them.

