## Standing invariants (inherited — do not relitigate)

- **License.** Every first-party file carries an `SPDX-License-Identifier` header set to
  `{{ license }}`.
{%- if license == "Apache-2.0" %}
  This repo is a **deliberate, reviewed Apache-2.0 exception** to the platform PolyForm
  default: it is genuinely open source. Keep `LICENSE`, `NOTICE` (if present), and the
  `REUSE.toml` annotation Apache-consistent. Preserve upstream notices on any vendored code.
{%- else %}
  This repo is **source-available for non-commercial use (PolyForm-Noncommercial-1.0.0)**.
  It is **not** open source. Never emit Apache/MIT headers, never call it "open source", and
  never relicense without an escalated, logged decision. Third-party/vendored material keeps
  its original license — never relabel it.
{%- endif %}
- **Python {{ python_version }}** for every command, venv, hook, script, and test. No fallback
  to system Python. `requires-python = ">={{ python_version }}"`; there is no 3.12 fallback —
  fix forward if a dependency breaks.
- **Issue-driven, branch + PR only.** Open an issue first for non-trivial work; branch from
  `main`; never commit directly to `main`. One thing per PR.
- **Quality gates are not theater.** Never lower a coverage floor, skip a test, add a blanket
  `noqa`, or weaken a gate to make it pass. A red gate is a bug to fix, not a baseline to accept.

## Standing process rules (enforced by the change-governance gate, not left to hope)

1. **Pressure-test in an isolated `/tmp` workstream**, never the shared checkout. HEAD-race with
   background agents corrupts the working tree; prove a change in `/tmp` (a throwaway clone or
   `git worktree`) before touching the real repo.
2. **Any non-surgical change requires a decision record before code.** "Non-surgical" = diff
   > ~150 LOC or > ~8 files, OR labelled `major`, OR touching a designated core path. The record
   lives in `docs/decisions/NNNN-*.md` (copy `docs/decisions/TEMPLATE.md`) and MUST contain a
   scored **A/B/C options comparison**, a **steelman** of the rejected options, and
   **pressure-test evidence** (log/link from the `/tmp` run). CI blocks the PR if it is missing
   or malformed.
3. **Major decisions get the A/B/C rating up front.** Before any large rewrite or new dependency,
   score the alternatives and record the winner — do not start typing the rewrite first.

## Build / test / gate commands

```
just gates          # full local gate suite (mirrors CI): lint, format, type, arch, test, sast, deps, reuse
just lint           # ruff check .
just format-check   # ruff format --check .
just typecheck      # mypy src/{{ module_name }} --strict
just arch           # import-linter architecture / import-boundary contracts
just test           # pytest --cov={{ module_name }} --cov-fail-under={{ coverage_min }} (unit + property)
just test-cli       # bats black-box CLI tests against the installed console script
just test-report    # pytest with Allure results (.allure-results)
just mutate         # opt-in mutation testing (mutmut) for security/validation code
just bandit         # bandit SAST
just pip-audit      # known-vulnerable dependency scan
just reuse-lint     # SPDX / license-header compliance
just secrets        # gitleaks secret scan
just release-gate   # local pre-release pre-flight: uv build + twine check + reuse lint
just skills-sync    # (re)install the skill set from the canonical skills library
just template-update# copier update — pull upstream template changes
```

Single test: `uv run pytest tests/test_smoke.py::test_main_returns_zero -q`

## Test harness

The scaffold ships a layered, mostly-black-box harness. Add to the tier that fits;
never weaken a floor to make a run green.

- **Unit** (`tests/test_*.py`, pytest) — fast, hermetic; the coverage floor
  (`--cov-fail-under={{ coverage_min }}`) is enforced here and in CI.
- **Property** (`tests/property/`, hypothesis) — invariants over generated inputs for pure
  functions (parsers, normalizers, encoders). State the invariant; let hypothesis break it.
- **Black-box CLI** (`tests/cli/*.bats`, bats-core) — drives the INSTALLED console script
  `{{ project_slug }}` (`--help` / `--version` / default) and asserts exit code + output.
  `just test-cli`. bats comes from the breachsafe-container image (`brew install bats-core`
  locally).
- **Architecture** (import-linter, `[tool.importlinter]` in `pyproject.toml`) — enforces the
  import-boundary contracts. `just arch`.
- **Reporting** (allure-pytest) — `just test-report` writes `.allure-results`; view with the
  Allure CLI bundled in the workbench image (`allure serve .allure-results`).
- **Fuzzing** (atheris, `tests/fuzz/`) — coverage-guided fuzzing of untrusted-input parsers;
  see `tests/fuzz/README.md`.
- **Mutation** (mutmut, opt-in) — `just mutate` proves the tests actually kill mutants; run it
  against security/validation-critical modules. Slow, so it is not part of `just gates`.

## CI

CI (`.github/workflows/ci.yml`) is a thin, **verbatim** (never Jinja-templated) shell: a
`load-config` job reads `.github/bqp.env` and passes `module` / `coverage_min` / `container_tag`
into the reusable quality-gate workflow
`{{ github_owner }}/breachsafe-golden-python/.github/workflows/quality-gates-python.yml@{{ golden_ref }}`,
which runs inside `ghcr.io/{{ github_owner }}/breachsafe-container:{{ container_tag }}`. A fix to
the gate logic lands once in breachsafe-golden-python and every repo inherits it on the next run.
Release is `.github/workflows/release.yml` (reusable `release-python.yml` — fail-closed gate, OIDC
publish, cosign, SLSA attestation).

## Security posture (OpenSSF Scorecard)

The repo ships a self-contained security-posture layer, all SHA-pinned and least-privilege:

- **OpenSSF Scorecard** (`.github/workflows/scorecard.yml`) — weekly + on `branch_protection_rule`;
  `publish_results: true` (needs a **public** repo). SARIF goes to the Security tab.
- **CodeQL** (`.github/workflows/codeql.yml`) — `security-extended` on push, PR, and weekly.
- **Fuzzing** — shared Atheris harnesses in `tests/fuzz/` feed two tiers:
  1. **ClusterFuzzLite** (`.github/workflows/cifuzz.yml` + `.clusterfuzzlite/`) runs in EVERY repo,
     per-PR, bounded, advisory (amd64 — atheris ships amd64-Linux wheels only).
  2. **Google OSS-Fuzz** (`oss-fuzz/`, generated for Apache repos only) — hosted continuous
     fuzzing. Requires a **one-time onboarding PR to google/oss-fuzz**; PolyForm repos are
     ineligible (OSS-Fuzz is OSS-only) and rely on ClusterFuzzLite. Write a harness once; both
     tiers consume it. Add one `fuzz_*.py` per untrusted-input boundary. See `tests/fuzz/README.md`.
- **Pinned dependencies.** Commit `uv.lock` (run `just lock`). Scorecard's Pinned-Dependencies
  check and CI's `uv sync --locked` both require a committed lockfile.
- **Branch protection** is scored by Scorecard; apply it as code with
  `breachsafe-golden-python/quality-gates/set_branch_protection.py` (requires a public repo or GitHub Pro).

